.TH APEXM 1 "July 2026" "apexm 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apexm \- Android APEX package manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apexm
\fI<operation>\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fItargets...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBapexm\fR is an Android APEX package manager for Linux. It resolves, downloads, and mounts APEX/CAPEX packages from Forgejo package registries. It supports dependency resolution by library name (with \fB\-l\fR), version pinning, optimal architecture selection, and user/root execution contexts.
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.BR install ", " \-S " (or " \-Sl ")"
Install packages and mount them. Requires target names. Use \-Sl to install by library name.
.TP
.BR remove ", " \-R
Remove installed packages and unmount them.
.TP
.BR search ", " \-Ss
Search configured repositories for packages matching the target.
.TP
.BR local ", " \-Qs " (or " \-Q " " \-s ", " local " " \-s ")"
Search locally installed packages matching the target.
.TP
.BR update ", " \-Su
Sync repository databases to get the latest package lists.
.TP
.BR download ", " \-Sd
Download packages without installing or mounting them.
.TP
.BR local ", " \-Q
Query locally installed packages matching the target library.
.TP
.BR list ", " \-\-list
List all installed packages.
.TP
.BR init ", " \-\-init
Re-mount all previously installed packages (useful after reboot).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Specify a custom configuration file path.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-library
Treat install targets as library names rather than package names.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-noconfirm
Skip interactive prompts (e.g. provider pickers) and auto-select defaults.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output for debugging.
.TP
.B \-\-isolated
Run in isolated mode for build environments, keeping everything local to the rootdir.
.TP
.BI \-\-rootdir " path"
Specify the base directory for APEX storage and mounts (default is /apex for root, ~/.apex for user).
.TP
.BI \-\-arch " architecture"
Force the tool to query a specific architecture.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-microarch " level"
Specify the highest microarchitecture level to download (e.g. v3 for x86_64).
.TP
.BI \-\-api-level " level" ", " \-\-api " level"
Specify the highest Android API level to download (upper bound / maximum API level).
.TP
.BI \-\-api-level-exact " level" ", " \-\-api-exact " level"
Filter packages strictly to an exact Android API level. Takes precedence over \fB\-\-api-level\fR and \fB\-\-api\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name
Show only package name or restrict target matching strictly to package name (do not search library dependencies).
.SH TARGET SYNTAX
Targets can be a package name (e.g., \fIcom.android.vulkan\fR).
When using the \fB\-l\fR or \fB\-\-library\fR flag, targets are treated as library names (e.g., \fIlibvulkan.so\fR).
.PP
Version Pinning: You can pin a specific versionCode by appending \fB@versionCode\fR to the target name.
.br
Example: \fBapexm install -Sl libvulkan.so@1300\fR
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B apexm
uses an INI-style configuration file to define Forgejo APEX registries. The tool searches all defined repositories in the order they appear. Repositories listed earlier have higher priority.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apex/repo.conf
System-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/apex/repo.conf
User-specific configuration file.
.TP
.I /apex/
Default system-wide mount point and storage directory (root mode).
.TP
.I ~/.apex/
Default user-specific mount point and storage directory (user mode).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mount (8),
.BR losetup (8)
